<speak>Let's start with appointments, because that's something I keep meaning to sort out. I prefer a telephone appointment to an unexpected call, especially when I'm at the business. If I know roughly when we're speaking, I can close the office door and keep the papers ready. Late morning is often crowded with staff questions, and the first part of the afternoon can be lunch with the family. Later in the afternoon is generally easier, provided we arrange it rather than leaving it to chance.</speak>